 "metadata": {
  "title": "Elementary population model",
  "description": "A population growing by births and shrinking by deaths, each a fixed fraction of its size each year; growth is exponential until the population reaches a ceiling, its carrying capacity, which it cannot exceed. Converted from the TrueBASIC program ELEMPOP.tru on the CD of the book.",
